<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bouvines</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1214">1214</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-french-war-1213-1214">Anglo-French War (1213–1214)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bouvines was fought on 27 July 1214 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lille">Lille</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip II of France</a> defeated the army of Emperor Otto IV, Count Ferrand of Flanders and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaud-de-dammartin">Renaud de Dammartin</a>, allies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. The victory secured French control of Normandy and Anjou, effectively ended Otto's reign and so weakened John that his barons forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-carta">Magna Carta</a> on him in 1215.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bouvines.jpg" alt="Battle of Bouvines" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Horace Vernet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_de_Bouvines_gagnee_par_Philippe_Auguste.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Count Ferrand was captured at the <b>Battle of Bouvines</b> in 1214, fighting in the coalition of Otto IV and King John of England against Philip II Augustus.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-flanders">County of Flanders · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The counts of Flanders and Hainaut were on the losing side at the <b>Battle of Bouvines</b> in 1214.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-hainaut">County of Hainaut · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…III commanded the French contingent of the Third Crusade after Philip II returned home in 1191 and died at Acre in 1192, Odo III fought for Philip II at the <b>Battle of Bouvines</b> in 1214, and Hugh IV joined the crusade of Louis IX to Egypt in 1248–1250.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Duchy of Burgundy · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Philip II Augustus conquered Normandy from King John of England in 1202–1204 and at the <b>Battle of Bouvines</b> in 1214 routed Emperor Otto IV and his Flemish allies.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>King John lost Normandy, Anjou and Maine to Philip II in 1202–1204, and his allies' defeat at <b>Bouvines</b> in 1214 ended hopes of recovery.</blockquote><a href="/state/angevin-empire">Angevin Empire</a></li><li><blockquote>Count Renaud de Dammartin fought against Philip II at <b>Bouvines</b> in 1214 and lost his lands.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-boulogne">County of Boulogne</a></li></ul></section>
